        "A simplified training process is: collect representative data; convert inputs into numerical features or representations; produce predictions; compare predictions with targets or another learning signal; calculate a loss; update model parameters; repeat; and evaluate on held-out data. The goal is generalization to unseen examples, not memorization of the training set.",
        "For spam detection, training data may contain message text, sender signals and metadata paired with spam/not-spam labels. The training algorithm adjusts parameters to reduce prediction error. During inference, a new email is passed through the trained model to obtain a prediction.",
